   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing, and I could not check it against the source. I assumed the wedge and hash types rather than reading them, so the stereodescriptors are the weakest part.\n\n**Skeleton, left to right**\n- A di\u2011tert\u2011butylsilylene ring (Si, two O, CH2, two CH) is fused to a tetrahydropyran.\n- That pyran is fused to an oxepane carrying a quaternary C\u2013Me.\n- Next come a tetrahydropyran, then an oxepane containing the ketone.\n- A CH2 links the ketone ring to a final tetrahydropyran. This ring bears an OPMB (O\u2013CH2\u2013C6H4\u2013OMe) group and an OBn group, plus a CH2CH2OBn side chain.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- Ring fusions are drawn trans, so I took the upper H's as wedges and the lower H's as hashes. The Me on the quaternary carbon is wedged.\n- The OPMB carbon is the least certain: I read its bond as hashed, so the O points away from the viewer.\n- I translated each centre into @/@@ by reading the neighbour order clockwise or counter-clockwise from the drawing coordinates.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)(C)[Si]1(C(C)(C)C)OC[C@@H]2O[C@@H]3CC[C@]4(C)O[C@@H]5C[C@@H]6O[C@H](C[C@@H]7O[C@H](CCOCc8ccccc8)[C@@H](OCc8ccccc8)C[C@@H]7OCc8ccc(OC)cc8)C(=O)CC[C@H]6O[C@H]5C[C@H]4O[C@H]3C[C@H]2O1"
